// Module 6 quiz - Deep Learning for AI Startups
$CATEGORY: $course$/Module 6

::M6 Q1:: What is an embedding? {
~A type of GPU
~A loss function
=A vector representing the meaning of text#An embedding model turns text into a list of numbers, so that texts with similar meaning get similar vectors.
~A dataset format
}

::M6 Q2:: Which metric is commonly used to compare embeddings? {
~Word count
=Cosine similarity#Cosine similarity measures the angle between two vectors, so it compares direction (meaning), not length.
~Batch size
~Dropout rate
}

::M6 Q3:: What problem does attention address? {
=Deciding which parts of the input matter for each position#Attention lets the model weigh how much each other word matters when it processes a given word.
~Compressing images
~Choosing a learning rate
~Labeling data
}

::M6 Q4:: Why split documents into chunks? {
~To hide data
~To remove embeddings
~To avoid using a model
=Models and retrieval work better on focused passages#One vector for a long page blurs many topics together, and models read only a limited amount of text.
}

::M6 Q5:: A query uses different words than the document but means the same. Which search finds it? {
~Exact keyword match only
~Alphabetical sort
=Semantic search with embeddings#Embeddings capture meaning, so a question and a passage with different words but the same meaning end up close together.
~Random sampling
}
